# zlib.vec — conformance vectors for the `zlib` family.
#
# ONE FILE, EVERY IMPLEMENTATION. The engine's src/Zlib.cpp and
# Compress::Zlib::Native's C are separate implementations on purpose — see
# NATIVE-MODULES-PLAN, "The architecture: independent C". This is what keeps
# them agreeing, so it is read by both and weakened by neither.
#
# THIS COPY IS THE MASTER. It moved here from Compress-Zlib-Native/t/vectors/
# when DATA-PLAN P4 landed and the engine became the primary implementation
# (NATIVE-MODULES-PLAN's order of work, step 1, whose other half moved with
# P3). The distribution keeps a copy so a published tarball stands alone;
# t/regression/data-native-zlib.raku checks the two are byte-identical whenever
# both are present.
#
# Generated by tools/gen-vectors.raku from real libz and the system gzip, never
# from our own code. Compression is not a function, so what is pinned is the
# direction that is: a stream a third party produced must inflate to exactly
# the bytes they compressed.
#
#   I <zlib|gzip|raw> <compressed-hex> <plain-hex>   must inflate to plain
#   X <zlib|gzip|raw> <compressed-hex>               must be REFUSED
#   C <crc32-hex>  <input-hex>
#   A <adler32-hex> <input-hex>
#
# `-` is the empty string in any of those fields.

I zlib 7801030000000001 -
I zlib 789c030000000001 -
I zlib 78da030000000001 -
I raw 000000ffff0300 -
I gzip 1f8b0800000000000013000000ffff03000000000000000000 -
C 00000000 -
A 00000001 -
